attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The initial velocity of a particle is $(5i+3j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the speed of the particle after $3$ seconds if the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(-i+2j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Round your answer to two decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"} {"question" "q-136355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=5i+3j,\\,a=-i+2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $3$ seconds, the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(5i+3j)+(-i+2j)(3) \\\\  & =(5i+3j)+(-3i+6j) \\\\  & =(2i+9j)\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v| & =|2i+9j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{9}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+81} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{85} \\\\  & ≈9.22\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"} {"question" "q-136355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "45dce97f8bb9919396f1ad7d4dbca8253ff1e7ddfe1478029c6481977473c035"} {"question" "q-136355" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" 