quation above, we can solve for $a,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 5i+13j & =(5i+j)+a(4) \\\\ 12j & =4a \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{4}(12j) \\\\  & =3j\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"} {"question" "q-136376" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "45dce97f8bb9919396f1ad7d4dbca8253ff1e7ddfe1478029c6481977473c035"} {"question" "q-136376" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"} {"question" "q-136376" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2j\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "-j\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "0\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "2i\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "3j\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"} {"question" "q-136376" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3j\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"} {"question" "q-317176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves with constant acceleration. The velocity of the particle equals $(-4i+9j)\\,\\text{ft/s}$ both when $t=0\\,\\text{s}$ and $t=7\\,\\text{s}.$ What is the acceleration of the particle?\n\n$a=($\n{{field-1}}$\\,i$\n$+$\n{{field-2}}$\\,j\\,)\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"} {"question" "q-317176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nu=-4i+9j,\\,v=-4i+9j,\\,t=7\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $a,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ -4i+9j & =(-4i+9j)+a(7) \\\\ 0 & =7a \\\\ a & =(0\\,i+0\\,j)\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"} {"question" "q-317176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "45dce97f8bb9919396f1ad7d4dbca8253ff1e7ddfe1478029c6481977473c035"} {"question" "q-317176" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"} {"question" "q-317176" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"} {"question" "q-317176" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"} {"question" "q-317176" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"} {"question" "q-319037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The initial velocity of a particle is $(2i+5j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the **exact** speed of the particle after $3$ seconds if the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(-3i+j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\n$|v|=$\n\n{{field-1}} $\\text{m/s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"} {"question" "q-319037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=2i+5j,\\,a=-3i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t=3\\,\\text{s},$ the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(2i+5j)+(-3i+j)(3) \\\\  & =(2i+5j)+(-9i+3j) \\\\  & =(-7\\,i+8\\,j)\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v| & =|-7i+8j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-7)^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{113}\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"} {"question" "q-319037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "45dce97f8bb9919396f1ad7d4dbca8253ff1e7ddfe1478029c6481977473c035"} {"question" "q-319037" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"} {"question" "q-319037" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{113}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"} {"question" "q-319169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(-2i+4j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}.$ The velocity of the particle is $(10i-8j)\\,\\text{km/h}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{h}.$ Find the time when the velocity of the particle equals $(-8i+28j)\\,\\text{km/h}.$\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,\\text{h}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"} {"question" "q-319169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nu=10i-8j,\\,v=-8i+28j,\\,a=-2i+4j,\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ -8i+28j & =10i-8j+(-2i+4j)t \\\\ -18i+36j & =(-2i+4j)t \\\\ -18i+36j & =-2ti+4tj\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the $i$ and $j$ components in the last equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-18=-2t \\\\ 36=4t\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,t=9\\,\\text{h}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"} {"question" "q-319169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "45dce97f8bb9919396f1ad7d4dbca8253ff1e7ddfe1478029c6481977473c035"} {"question" "q-319169" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"} {"question" "q-319169" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044345/state.json" "file_sha256" "deed94b0ef66ef7a3cf9f94b53bdbfaaa5f7d0db4f5d999eb3995eca3ae2f4df"}] "usage" {"q-317176" []} "basis" 1657 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186286072 17592186286074] "immutable_fields" [[17592186286071 :answer-field/correct] [17592186286071 :answer-field/id] [17592186286071 :answer-field/key] [17592186286071 :answer-field/type] [17592186286073 :answer-field/correct] [17592186286073 :answer-field/id] [17592186286073 :answer-field/key] [17592186286073 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
